<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="3JN" style="id">3 JOHN</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="3JN 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="3JN 1:1"/>
    The Elder,
    <verse eid="3JN 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">To Gaius, my beloved, whom I sincerely love in the truth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="3JN 1:2"/>
    Beloved, I pray that you may prosper in every respect and remain in good health, just as your inner life is thriving.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="3JN 1:3"/>
    I rejoiced greatly when brothers and sisters came and testified to your faithfulness to the truth, how you continue to live in accordance with it.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="3JN 1:4"/>
    I have no greater joy than to hear that my children are walking in the truth.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Commendation of Gaius</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="3JN 1:5"/>
    Beloved, you are acting faithfully in all that you do for the brothers and sisters, even when they are strangers to you.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="3JN 1:6"/>
    They have borne witness before the church to your love. You will do well to send them on their way in a manner worthy of God.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="3JN 1:7"/>
    For they went out for the sake of the Name, accepting nothing from unbelievers.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="3JN 1:8"/>
    Therefore, we ought to support such people, so that we may become fellow workers for the truth.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Diotrephes and Demetrius</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="3JN 1:9"/>
    I wrote something to the church, but Diotrephes, who desires to put himself first, does not accept our authority.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="3JN 1:10"/>
    For this reason, if I come, I will bring attention to his actions, how he spreads malicious accusations against us. Not content with this, he refuses to receive the brothers and sisters, and he hinders those who desire to do so, even expelling them from the church.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="3JN 1:11"/>
    Beloved, do not imitate what is evil, but what is good. The one who does good belongs to God; the one who does evil has not seen God.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="3JN 1:12"/>
    Demetrius has received a good testimony from everyone, and even from the truth itself. We also bear witness to him, and you know that our testimony is true.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Farewell Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="3JN 1:13"/>
    I have many things to write to you, but I do not wish to write them with pen and ink.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="3JN 1:14"/>
    Instead, I hope to see you soon, and we will speak face to face.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="3JN 1:15"/>
    Peace be to you. The friends greet you. Greet the friends there individually by name.
    <verse eid="3JN 1:15"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="3JN 1"/>
</usx>
